## Sunflower oil
component-sunflower-oil = Sunflower oil
component-sunflower-oil-made-of-part = fats (triglycerides of linoleic and oleic acids)
component-sunflower-oil-decomposes-into = smoke and breakdown products
component-sunflower-oil-description-novice = Oil does not boil like water: heated long enough, at ≈ 232 °C (refined) it starts to smoke and break down.
component-sunflower-oil-description-school = By estimate, oil has about half the specific heat of water, so it heats about twice as fast. It is lighter than water (≈ 919 kg/m³) and conducts heat about 3.5 times worse.
component-sunflower-oil-safety-school = Hot oil causes severe burns, and water that gets into hot oil makes it spatter. Burning oil is never put out with water.
component-sunflower-oil-model-notes = We found no data on how sunflower oil solidifies, so in the model it does not.
